{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And you shall say: men of livestock.</b> Joseph was concerned that if they become officials in Pharaoh's house, they might bring him down from his greatness — for on account of envy over the striped tunic they sold him." "<b>For it is an abomination of Egypt.</b> Rashi explained: because they are elohim to them. Their object of fear was the sign of the ram, and on its account they would worship it. 'Abomination of Egypt' — the object of fear of Egypt, like 'Moab's abomination' and 'abomination of the children of Ammon.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {1 "The parenthetical correction '(אין)[הן]' replaces אין with הן, reflecting that sheep/shepherds are elohim to the Egyptians; the translation follows הן."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:52.757873192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}